# 🔴 THE FAILURE THIS PREVENTS, measured 2026-09-05 on a real Windows install.
# Git on Windows converts line endings on checkout by default, so every shell
# script arrived with CRLF and bash could not read them:
#
#     /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#
# ⛔ ALL THREE GATES WERE DEAD — and `git` read the failing hook as exit 0, so a
# commit that should have been refused went through. ⚠️ A gate that dies quietly
# is worse than no gate: the person believes they are protected.
#
# ⭐ A shell script is not text to be adapted to the platform: it is a program
# whose interpreter rejects the carriage return. Same for Python, which git
# would also convert.

# Everything the engine executes keeps LF, on every platform.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf

# ⚠️ The commands in bin/ carry no extension and git cannot infer them.
bin/*       text eol=lf
hooks/*     text eol=lf
Mente/bin/*     text eol=lf
Mente/hooks/*   text eol=lf

# Documents may follow the platform; nothing executes them.
*.md        text
*.tsv       text
*.yml       text
*.json      text
